  "question": {
    "text": "An organization awarded <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>48</mn></math> medals in event <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>A</mi><none/><mo>'</mo><mprescripts/><none/><mo>'</mo></mmultiscripts></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math> in event <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>B</mi><none/><mo>'</mo><mprescripts/><none/><mo>'</mo></mmultiscripts></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn></math> in event <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><none/><mo>'</mo><mprescripts/><none/><mo>'</mo></mmultiscripts></math>. If these medals went to total <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn></math> men and only five men got medals in all the three events, then, how many received medals in exactly two of three events?",
    "image": null
  },
