  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> denote the set of men who received medals in even <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>, event <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and event&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p><p>Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>C</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>&nbsp;,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>,</p><p>Now we know that,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>C</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math></p><p>Therefore, the number of people who received medals in exactly two of the three sports will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math>.</p>",
